This patch does two things: firstly, it alters the proficiency checks
for bullwhip effects (disarming etc.) so that they rely more on weapon
skill than pure dexterity. More importantly, when you snap a bullwhip
at an empty adjacent space, there is a chance (made increasingly
certain with extra proficiency) that you will CRACK the bullwhip,
causing all animals adjacent to you to flee. (Do you think this effect
is useful enough?)

